# Copy to .env and fill in for anything beyond local development.
# Never commit the real .env file, and never hardcode a private key in
# source (hardhat.config.js, deploy.js, registerCredential.js all read
# these from the environment for exactly this reason).

# --- Local development (default) ---
# Nothing needs to be set here. `localhost` network uses the Hardhat node's
# own well-known test accounts, which is fine ONLY because that node is
# local and not reachable by anyone else.

# --- Any real network (testnet/mainnet) ---
# RPC endpoint for the target network (e.g. an Infura/Alchemy URL).
# SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=

# Private key of the account that deploys the contract and becomes its
# owner (accreditation authority). Fund this address with enough native
# token to cover deployment gas. NEVER the local Hardhat test mnemonic.
# DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Private key of the account the backend uses to call registerCredential().
# Must be accredited on-chain first (the deployer is auto-accredited; grant
# this one too via registry.accreditIssuer(address) if it's different).
# ISSUER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Overrides the address auto-read from deployed.json, if needed.
# CONTRACT_ADDRESS=

# Overrides who becomes the contract's owner at deploy time (defaults to
# the deployer's own address).
# OWNER_ADDRESS=
